From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: x18-patch every instruction that reads x18

The patcher sent loads, stores, ADD/SUB and MOV off x18 to a TEB
trampoline. Every other instruction that reads x18 kept reading the 0 iOS
leaves there: World of Warcraft's ARM64 client mixes x18 into opaque
predicates and computed values in any data-processing form (TST, EOR,
CCMP, CSEL, MADD, CBZ ...), and with 0 for the TEB those went their other
way.

ios_insn_x18_role now returns the fields holding x18 as a source for the
logical (register and immediate), ADD/SUB, ADC/SBC, CCMP/CCMN, CSEL,
1- and 2-source, 3-source, bitfield and EXTR classes, a store of x18 and
LDP/STP's second register; each of those fields gets the scratch register.
CBZ/CBNZ/TBZ/TBNZ on x18 get a trampoline that branches on the TEB and
ends in a B to the original target or back. Forms where register 31 is SP
(a destination without S, a store relative to SP) are left alone, as the
trampoline moves SP. A word read by a literal load stays code whenever it
reads x18 with Rd = 31, as 0260 did for CMP: such a word is odd, so no
aligned pointer.

Linear: PLA-514
Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 229 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 157 insertions(+), 72 deletions(-)

